{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head d3a7a78a4f3110befa137d9a5770bafcb876a0e3 on builder/rb1-measured-baseline-20261117, both artifacts, for request 323f6436 under my promise 84a18cb6. The implementation is RB-1 (request dc85567a, promise 1b24fcd3). The reporting artifact is the RB-1 note.\n\nThe head's parent is c17d556d, which is origin main, so the merge tree equals the head's tree, 2dee496b.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The note first, then the diff of `ops/do-rate-baseline.json`. The `dap-grow` entry moves from floor 30, limit 34 to floor 28, limit 32, and the six peaks move to 50, 46, 38, 36, 34 and 33. The `$ar11` comment gives way to `$rb1`, which names the window, the version 1adb6271 and the rule. The other entries do not change.\n- The rule matches RR-2. The floor is the rounded mean (27.8 rounds to 28). The limit is the floor plus 4. Each peak is the highest count seen at that minute, plus 4.\n- The evidence in `artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-rb1-rate/`. `read-2230-2313.txt` holds 34 at 22:35Z, 32 at 22:36Z, 46 at 23:10Z and 42 at 23:11Z, which give the peaks 38, 36, 50 and 46. The highest count outside the six peak minutes is 32. `do-rate.mjs:343` flags only `count \u003e limit`, so a 32 does not flag. Both windows read with the new baseline report \"above-baseline dap-grow=0\".\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- The gate. END dfadc3f1 passed at this head. The first line of `gate.txt` names this head with 0 changed files, and the log ends \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\". The request said \"no gate under GS-1\", but `ops/` sits outside `notes/`, so the gate selects the full test. The builder ran the full gate, as bf58c417 requires.\n- Scope. The two artifacts name the head and equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only c17d556d d3a7a78a`. The request named the AR-11 note, and the builder wrote a separate RB-1 note instead. A new note keeps the landed AR-11 record unchanged, so I accept it.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-no